From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(AudioManager): a volume above zero clears a mute

set_volume() sets the level only. WirePlumber keeps a sink's mute in its
saved state and restores it at every boot, so a speaker muted by any
client stayed silent while the volume slider and keys moved the level
(HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24: muted from an unknown source, silent
across reboots and an update).

Once the volume is set above zero, the sink is unmuted too, as desktop
volume controls do. A volume of zero leaves the mute as it is, and the
mute key still toggles it.

---
 core/global/audio_manager.gd | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed

--- a/core/global/audio_manager.gd
+++ b/core/global/audio_manager.gd
@@ -82,6 +82,15 @@
 	cmd.execute()
 	var code := await cmd.finished as int
 	
+	# A volume above zero also clears a mute, as desktop volume controls do: a mute set elsewhere
+	# (another client, or one WirePlumber restored at boot) otherwise stayed through every change.
+	if code == 0 and current_volume > 0:
+		_muted = false
+		var unmute := Command.create("wpctl", ["set-mute", "@DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@", "0"])
+		unmute.timeout = 5.0
+		unmute.execute()
+		code = await unmute.finished as int
+
 	return code
 
 
